The narrow-viewport layout - everything gated on viewport geometry (the
narrowGate overlay), independent of touch: a phone-width window shows one
workbench part fullscreen at a time.

- layout.ts: NARROW_PARTS fullscreen switching; boot pass seeds intent from
  the restored layout (parts restored visible fire no visibility event, so
  the first narrow pass would otherwise close what the user left open);
  rotation preserves the selected part; narrow close-part events from
  shell.js dismiss the fullscreen part on back gestures.
- Titlebar: the left flex region shrinks below the menubar's intrinsic width
  and the menubar flexes from zero, so MenuBar measures its real allocation
  and moves labels into overflow instead of pushing the title off-screen.
- Extension editor: feature tables get a picker (styled by narrow.css) and
  horizontal scrolling, so wide columns stay reachable.

